LeetCode 127. Word Ladder
Problem Statement

You are given:

beginWord → Starting word
endWord → Target word
wordList → Dictionary of valid words

You can transform one word into another by:

Changing exactly one letter
The new word must exist in the dictionary

Return the length of the shortest transformation sequence from beginWord to endWord.

If it's impossible, return 0.

Example
Input
beginWord = "hit"

endWord = "cog"

wordList =

["hot","dot","dog","lot","log","cog"]
Valid Transformation
hit
 ↓
hot
 ↓
dot
 ↓
dog
 ↓
cog

Length

hit -> hot -> dot -> dog -> cog

Total words = 5

Output

5
Invalid Example
beginWord = "hit"

endWord = "cog"

wordList =
["hot","dot","dog","lot","log"]

Notice

cog

is missing.

Therefore,

Output

0
Why BFS?

The question asks for the shortest transformation.

Whenever a problem asks for

Shortest path
Minimum steps
Minimum operations

think of

Breadth First Search (BFS)

Because BFS explores level by level.

Graph Representation

Think of every word as a node.

Example

hit
 |
hot
/  \
dot lot
|    |
dog  log
 \   /
  cog

Each edge means

These two words differ by exactly one character.

We need the shortest path from

hit

to

cog
High Level Idea

Instead of comparing every word with every other word,

For each current word,

Try changing

first letter
second letter
third letter
...

to every character

a...z

If the new word exists in dictionary,

it becomes our next BFS node.

Step 1

Convert List into HashSet

Set<String> wordSet = new HashSet<>(wordList);

Why?

Searching inside a List

contains(word)

Time = O(N)

Searching inside HashSet

contains(word)

Time = O(1)

Huge performance improvement.

